'''Ash's house''' is where [[Ash Ketchum]] lives with his mother [[Delia]], and their shared {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} [[Mimey]] reside in. The house is located in [[Pallet Town]] in the [[Kanto]] [[region]].

After turning ten years old and obtaining his [[Pokémon Trainer's license]], Ash departed from home to embark on his [[Pokémon journey]]. Due to Ash being on the road for long periods of time, Delia lived at the house alone until the events of ''[[EP064|It's Mr. Mime Time]]'' when Mimey was {{pkmn2|caught}} by Ash and left to reside with Delia, where it helps with cleaning and vacuuming the house. The house is where Ash returns to after the end of each journey, and very rarely during the middle of his journey as depicted from ''It's Mr. Mime Time'' to ''[[EP073|Bad To The Bone]]'', when Ash and {{ashfr}} spent a few months in Pallet Town (while occasionally traveling elsewhere in-between) in preparation for the [[Indigo Plateau Conference]].

The house also been host for other guests besides the Ketchum family, such as {{an|Misty}}, {{an|Brock}}, {{an|Professor Oak}}, [[Tracey Sketchit]], {{an|May}}, {{an|Max}}, [[Professor Birch]], {{an|Alexa}}, [[Goh]], and [[Chloe]]. 

